  "method": "Sent through one MIDI input with nothing read back, then read through the other after the cable was moved. Every stimulus carried a value used by no other stimulus in the run, so a byte that differs from the baseline and holds one of those values names the message that wrote it.",
  "values_are_unique": "Two stimuli sent at one value would be indistinguishable afterwards, and the run would credit whichever of them the table happened to keep. The values are checked for uniqueness before anything is sent rather than chosen carefully and trusted.",
  "nothing_was_restored": "The first phase leaves everything it wrote in place, because what it wrote is the only thing that survives the cable move. A restore would put the unit back and take the measurement with it. The second phase resets the unit once it has read what it came for.",
